```

So the persisted `registrationDate` is: default-to-today if absent, reject if future, then rolled forward over weekends/holidays. Every downstream date-derived value (membershipNumber year, tenure, ageBand, daily-limit, bulk-signup) reads this already-adjusted date.

Consumers of the adjusted registration date:
- `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded.java:20-22` — rejects create when ≥100 owners share the adjusted date. Class `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded`, single method `service`, constant `DAILY_LIMIT=100`.
