## How the pieces connect (create/read flow)

1. `BuildOwner.service` normalises input, defaults/validates `registrationDate`, and applies `BusinessDay.rollForward` → stores the business-day-adjusted date on the `Owner`.
2. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service` sets `customerCode` = `Locality.of(owner)` + `-` + hash.
3. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded` / `BulkSignup` use the adjusted `registrationDate` for per-day counts.
4. On response, `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (lines 21-33) fills derived DTO fields via expression mappings, including `MembershipNumber.of` (uses `registrationDate.getYear()`), `CheckDigit.of`, `Locality.of`, `Timezone.of`, `AgeBand.of`.
5. `RespondWithOwner` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` additionally compute `MembershipLevel.points/level` (tenure via 365-day window) and set them on the DTO; `RespondWithOwnerCreated` also emits the AUDIT log with `MembershipNumber.of`.

**Bonus date-derived value (item "any date-derived values"):**
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AgeBand.java` — class `AgeBand`, single method `of(Owner)`. Computes age via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` → `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`. This is another date-derived field (line 24) that also keys off `registrationDate`.

**Data model:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — `registrationDate` (line 100, getter 125) and `birthDate` (line 103) are the `LocalDate` sources for every derivation above. (Owner is a large JavaBean; its methods are all trivial getters/setters plus pet-collection helpers — not relevant to complexity of the derivations.)

